<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 1.705 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 1.705 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico had assigned two of three direct Cetes sales whereby it had sought to drain 1.705 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The auctions were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>	AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE</p>
<p>	150 million    356 days    22.93 pct</p>
<p>	150 million    181 days    21.75 pct</p>
<p>	150 million     90 days</p>
<p>Banco de Mexico also offered two repurchase agreements as follows:</p>
<p>    1.000 bln	6 days</p>
<p>	255 million	3 days    *Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
